.TH WERKMEISTER-MACHINE-TOKENS 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-machine\-tokens \- List daemon tokens with no workspace; \-\-remove deletes them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister machine tokens\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
Delete the stale tokens (default: list only)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBWhat it does:\fR
.IP 1. 3
Lists the files in \fB~/.werkmeister/tokens\fR whose name is not a folder under the workspaces root (\fBpaths.workspaces_root\fR)
.IP 2. 3
With \fB\-\-remove\fR, deletes them. A workspace's own token is never touched
.PP
Without \fB\-\-remove\fR nothing changes. If the workspaces root cannot be read or holds no workspace folder, nothing is removed and the command exits 1.
.PP
\fBWhen to use:\fR
.IP \(bu 3
Once after upgrading past 0.74.0: core tests that ran before SW\-433 left tokens there (see the release notes for the name prefixes)
.IP \(bu 3
After deleting a workspace folder by hand
.PP
A removed token is minted again by the next \fBwerkmeister workspace init\fR for that workspace.
.PP
A workspace that lives outside the workspaces root counts as stale: keep \fBpaths.workspaces_root\fR correct before using \fB\-\-remove\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
